.TH CHTTPSVR_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_declare_scoped \- declare a chttpsvr variable with automatic destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr_declare_scoped(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Works like chttpsvr_declare, but also attaches a GCC cleanup
attribute, so the server is destroyed automatically, exactly as
chttpsvr_destroy would destroy it, when name goes out of scope.  The
macro initializes the variable to CHTTPSVR_INVALID, and the cleanup
does nothing if name holds that value at the end of the scope.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_construct_scoped (3),
.BR chttpsvr_declare (3)
